## Research Paper 6

### Title
A Secure Adversarial Attack Detector Framework for Monitoring Network Intrusion in IoT Environment

### Authors
P. Verma, A. Vidyarthi, A. Mishra, J. Ali, N. Bharot, and J. G. Breslin

### Year
2025

### Research Problem
The study investigated the vulnerability of network intrusion detection in IoT environments when machine-learning models are exposed to adversarial attacks. The researchers also examined defensive approaches for improving robustness against adversarial manipulation.

### Method / Technique
The research investigated multiple adversarial attacks and used defensive mechanisms including adversarial training and adversarial attack detection.

### Dataset / Tools
The study focused on machine-learning-based network intrusion detection in an IoT environment and evaluated multiple adversarial attack and defense techniques.

### Main Findings
The study demonstrated that adversarial defenses can improve intrusion-detection robustness. However, the effectiveness of the defense was not equal across all adversarial attacks. This indicates that strong protection against one attack does not necessarily guarantee the same level of protection against another attack.

### Limitations
The study focused on an IoT intrusion-detection framework and used a broader defensive approach. It did not specifically isolate FGSM-only adversarial training using Logistic Regression on CIC-IDS2017 followed by testing against FGSM, JSMA, and DeepFool.

### Relevance to Our Research
This paper is important because it supports the cross-attack generalisation problem addressed by our research. The different defensive results across attacks suggest that robustness against one adversarial technique cannot automatically be assumed to generalise to another. Our research investigates this issue directly by training the defense using FGSM and testing it against both seen and unseen attacks.

### Reference
Verma, P., Vidyarthi, A., Mishra, A., Ali, J., Bharot, N., & Breslin, J. G. (2025). A secure adversarial attack detector framework for monitoring network intrusion in IoT environment. *IEEE Transactions on Consumer Electronics, 71*(4), 11613–11623.

